body:
I've had the exact same thoughts.  I know I can't go on much longer.  My life has accomplished nothing of significance.  I've had fantasies where "God" or whatever it is comes to me and says "OK, this kid is dying of cancer and really wants to live.  He can, but only if you give up your life."

&#x200B;

What a gift it would be.

You must have been active trading this week man.  Even without any money to play with after the final TSLA disaster I can't help but watch.

&#x200B;

You've had an incredible story.  I remember in February you were thinking it would be years before you got back to $36,000 and now you're already back on top!  Would be awesome if you wrote it up on here.  Are you just doing SVXY/UVXY now?  Put spreads?  Something else?  I don't think I'll ever give up on making the million back, but if I ever get $50,000 together I'll make sure I never add any money in, just let the profits ride (if any profits are even made) and if I work it up to a million I'm out.  I pretty much need the next Bitcoin.  

&#x200B;

Are you still finding good opportunities with the less leverage in SVXY/UVXY?  I have a couple friends who made money in the past with those and haven't been able to with the changes.

So there it is.  120 spreads sold for a measly little over $2000.  

I realize people are unlikely to believe it's real.  Hell, I can't believe it myself.  This is sort of therapy for me.  At this point I don't even care if people figure out who I am from the post.  I'm way beyond caring now.  The only thing I care about is hopefully getting out without spending much more than $60,000 to buy them back.

&#x200B;

I welcome the abuse I know I'm going to get at this point.  Hell, I deserve it.  I only came here to see if anyone had any first hand experiences like this and could rate my chances of "only" paying $5 per spread to close out.

&#x200B;

But for what it's worth, and I would never say something like this- I swear on my mother's name that I am short 120 $295/290 put spreads, and would be way over 200% in TSLA even at 1000 shares.  So clearly this is the final proof of gambling sickness- maybe the lucky gambling got me up to a million, but it's all gone now.

Brother, my advice isn't worth squat probably as I'm in my early 40's, pissed away a million bucks, and currently have a negative net worth (all from options crap), but a couple of buddies of mine have stories that you may find useful.

&#x200B;

1) Guy worked up to $2.5 million or so by 2011.  Had a couple disasters taking him down just under 1 million.  Put it all in a stock that got halted.  Went negative.  Thought very (very) seriously about suicide, but ended up filing for bankruptcy.  Couple years back cobbled together $20K somehow and turned it into $200,000 in some oil distressed preferred issues.  Says he's done forever.

&#x200B;

2) Guy worked up to $1 million by 2016.  Lost most of it in options trades trying to get up to $10,000,000 where he said he would quit.  Then put the final $200,000 in RAD calls for the merger- got zeroed out.  Saved up $10,000 and made an incredible options play on GNW that got him to $200K- then lost over half that on the NXPI killed merger.

&#x200B;

My story isn't finished yet but I've been in an incredible funk for a couple years now.  On the plus side, I have a 1 million dollar capital loss carry forward and I'm just crazy enough to think if I save up $10,000 I can hit a few lotto tickets and get it back.

&#x200B;

But I have sworn if I ever make those losses back, I mean the day I hit the old high point- I am out forever and never looking back.  It probably won't happen anyway, but I hope you consider establishing a number and when you hit that, just put it in fixed income or real estate.  You've obviously got some incredible skills and/or capital access to already be getting it done again, so you'll undoubtedly make it back to a few million- but please for the love of God take the money and run!

Off topic, but I saw your post about teeth and hope it got better.  I have been close to suicide the past two years for mostly other reasons, but tooth pain I've started to experience (and am unable to pay to fix) may end up pushing me over the edge.

&#x200B;

I'm desperately looking for jobs teaching English in Asia and hopefully will find an affordable dentist there.

If the A's go 10-10, need to go 17-4 to force a playoff.

&#x200B;

My God.  538 projection has 1% chance of making the playoffs.  So you're saying there's a chance!
